E02-NB-005 (retained, non-blocking, observation): attempts accounting asymmetry between terminal paths still present (scheduler.ts:122 vs 162).\"],\"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\":[],\"readinessAssessment\":\"Both canonical blockers are fixed in their ruled scope and the fixes verify independently. EPIC-02-BLOCK-001: per-SDK-instance seam via AsyncLocalStorage (shared/context.ts InstanceSeam/runWithInstanceSeam/resolveInstancePoke; sdk.ts scopeSurface wraps intakeStream/messages/turns/work.drain; enqueue's poke rides ctx.poke) matches the per-instance-scoping ruling; the required regression tests exist and pass (test/epic-fix-02.test.ts, background-then-manual and manual-then-background, manual rows stay queued until explicit drain with a live-background positive control). The module-global slots survive only as a documented below-SDK default for direct non-SDK calls — a recorded deviation from the literal 'replace the slots' wording that cannot auto-drain a manual SDK (every manual sdk.* operation runs in the no-op seam); the unscoped sdk.threads surface is benign (no threads public operation opens a thread database — all openThreadDatabase callers are scoped surfaces or the scheduler). EPIC-02-BLOCK-002a: findPairedBlock and findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary now join message with deleted_at IS NULL; regression test proves a deleted result's call summary rebuilds outcome 'unknown'. EPIC-02-BLOCK-002b: edit and message-delete cascades clear+requeue the live pair counterpart; TC-6.2's cascade-scope assertion was amended per the recorded ruling with the red-manifest hash re-recorded (test-immutability passes); the cascade-scope clarification is recorded in the impl log (fix-batch item 4). Gates re-run independently: pnpm run verify-all exit 0 (build, typecheck, lint 76 files, boundaries, 30 test files / 234 tests including the 3 new regression tests) and pnpm run green-verify exit 0 (27 Red-phase files unchanged). However, the ruling's application is incomplete: cascadeTurnDelete — one of the three mutation close paths sharing the one cascade module — leaves a dynamically-reproduced stale-outcome path (REVERIFY-02-001), so the candidate cannot cleanly close against its own recorded cascade contract. Process notes for closeout: both epic-fix harness envelopes errored (PROVIDER_STALLED / PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID) even though the fix work landed in the tree; the entire fix batch is uncommitted working-tree state; an unrelated Epic 03 spec edit (docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md) also sits uncommitted in the tree and should not ride an Epic 02 closeout commit. The four retained non-blocking findings stand as recorded and do not gate closeout.\",\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Run one small follow-up fix batch: extend cascadeTurnDelete to include pairedCounterpartSubject for each deleted member message whose live counterpart lies outside the deleted turn (dedupe against the drop set), add a cross-turn regression test (call in t1, late result in t2 via AC-2.8, delete t2 → t1 call summary cleared and requeued at the next source version, rebuilds outcome 'unknown'), re-run green-verify/verify-all, then commit fix-batch-001 plus this follow-up (excluding the unrelated Epic 03 doc edit) and re-run the reverify pass.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/002-epic-reverify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T09:29:15.642Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T09:39:40.500Z\"}\n","numLines":2,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2}}}
