{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DM7ZvufMmJwshHXAii6Fjo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Epic 02 Fix Batch 002 — spec-vs-build review findings (external reviewer report, impl-lead verified)\n2\t\n3\tConstraints for the whole batch: no schema changes; no new dependencies; do not touch sanctioned-pivot behavior (live-work-only queue rows, update-only completion, source-version discard, CLI provider resolution, drainSettled(ThreadRef)); full suite green including LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 before closing; Fix 1's new test runs in the default suite, not behind the process flag. Note: scheduler seams are now per-SDK-instance (epic-fix-001) — wire the Fix 1 timer per instance, not via module globals.\n4\t\n5\t- [ ] **Fix 1 (P2): Background backoff stall — scheduler never wakes for eligible_at.** In background mode, when a drain pass ends with `stoppedBecause: \"waiting\"`, schedule a wake at the report's `waitingUntil` (`setTimeout` clamped to a sane minimum) that runs through the existing single-flight/coalesce poke path. At most one pending wake per thread — a poke or newer wake replaces/clears the old timer; `unref()` the timer so it never keeps the process alive; clear timers on drainSettled completion paths and any dispose/shutdown. Manual mode unchanged: `waiting` stays a terminal drain outcome with no timers. Use the SDK clock seam for computing the delay where applicable (do not worsen recorded deviation E02-NB-001). Test: background SDK, backoffBaseMs ~25ms, provider fails retryably once then succeeds; await `drainSettled` with no external poke after the failure → form `ready`, attempts = 2, elapsed ≥ backoff delay; companion negative asserts no retry ran before `eligible_at`. Existing manual-mode waiting tests (work-execution.test.ts) stay as-is.\n6\t- [ ] **Fix 2 (P2): Tool-run grouping in turn rendering (AC-3.4 / Story 3 anti-shim restoration).** In `composeRenderingInput` (src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts), group maximal runs of consecutive tool activity (tool_call/tool_result in record order, unbroken by prompts or assistant text; thinking and runtime notes do NOT break a run — record that decision in the story deviation table). Each run becomes ONE RenderingPart and ONE receipt: tools used, call count, per-call mechanical outcomes joined into a run-level account; mixed outcomes stay explicit (e.g. \"2 succeeded, 1 failed: <reason>\"), never collapsed into vague success. Outcomes remain record-derived from derived_form.metadata (mechanical stamping untouched); non-tool parts unchanged. Check src/providers/deterministic.ts join still produces sensible output with grouped parts; adjust only if the input contract changed shape. Tests: turn with prompt, call, result, call, result, text, call, result → exactly two tool-run parts (sizes 2 and 1), receipts outcome-explicit; rendering contains run accounts and does NOT contain one entry per tool message; add a mixed-outcome run case naming the failure. Ripple: confirm chunk-summary tests still pass after re-derivation (no recorded goldens exist; the double derives from input).\n7\t- [ ] **REVERIFY-02-001 (blocking-candidate): cascadeTurnDelete missing pair-counterpart cascade.** The epic-fix-001 ruling (call/result pair is a source dependency; deleting one half is a source change for the counterpart's summary) was applied to cascadeFromMessage and cascadeMessageDelete but not cascadeTurnDelete (src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts:279-306). Cross-turn pairs are reachable (late result lands in a later turn; AC-2.8 repair rebuilds the earlier call summary). In cascadeTurnDelete, collect the paired-counterpart subjects for each deleted member message — skipping counterparts that are themselves members of the deleted turn, deduped — and clear + requeue their tool-activity summaries in the same transaction, exactly as the other two cascade paths do. Add a cross-turn regression test: call in t1, late result in t2 (summary rebuilt 'succeeded'), deleteTurn(t2) → t1's call summary cleared/requeued, rebuilds to 'unknown'.\n8\t- [ ] **Fix 3.1 (P3): Story 3 chunk-max doc fix.** stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md line ~124: change \"max 8000\" to \"max 4400\" — tech-design DD-9, §Interfaces, and sdk.ts defaults all say 4400; the story is the outlier.\n9\t- [ ] **Fix 3.2 (P3): TC-2.7 thinking coverage.** Add an assistant_thinking message to the existing TC-2.7 test in test/derivation-messages.test.ts: assert no work rows queued and no derivation state rows for it.\n10\t- [ ] **Fix 3.3 (P3): Delete-side stale-straggler test.** Add a test (mutations-delete.test.ts or the natural home): claim a work item for a form on the target, delete the target (messages.deleteMessage or turns.deleteTurn), complete the stale claimed item → assert it discards (`stale_discarded`), tombstone and cascade state intact.\n11\t- [ ] **Record Fix 1 and Fix 2** in the tech-design deviation table / story 3 deviation table as applicable: Fix 1 as a design completion (DD-4 background scheduling honors eligibility), Fix 2 as spec-compliance restoration (not a deviation).\n12\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0237ebdd-fed4-43b7-aea6-2688595304fb","uuid":"8b30afc0-6933-4ce7-8dd5-1d079d80758b","timestamp":"2026-06-11T10:28:53.314Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/fix-batch-002.md","content":"# Epic 02 Fix Batch 002 — spec-vs-build review findings (external reviewer report, impl-lead verified)\n\nConstraints for the whole batch: no schema changes; no new dependencies; do not touch sanctioned-pivot behavior (live-work-only queue rows, update-only completion, source-version discard, CLI provider resolution, drainSettled(ThreadRef)); full suite green including LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 before closing; Fix 1's new test runs in the default suite, not behind the process flag. Note: scheduler seams are now per-SDK-instance (epic-fix-001) — wire the Fix 1 timer per instance, not via module globals.\n\n- [ ] **Fix 1 (P2): Background backoff stall — scheduler never wakes for eligible_at.** In background mode, when a drain pass ends with `stoppedBecause: \"waiting\"`, schedule a wake at the report's `waitingUntil` (`setTimeout` clamped to a sane minimum) that runs through the existing single-flight/coalesce poke path. At most one pending wake per thread — a poke or newer wake replaces/clears the old timer; `unref()` the timer so it never keeps the process alive; clear timers on drainSettled completion paths and any dispose/shutdown. Manual mode unchanged: `waiting` stays a terminal drain outcome with no timers. Use the SDK clock seam for computing the delay where applicable (do not worsen recorded deviation E02-NB-001). Test: background SDK, backoffBaseMs ~25ms, provider fails retryably once then succeeds; await `drainSettled` with no external poke after the failure → form `ready`, attempts = 2, elapsed ≥ backoff delay; companion negative asserts no retry ran before `eligible_at`. Existing manual-mode waiting tests (work-execution.test.ts) stay as-is.\n- [ ] **Fix 2 (P2): Tool-run grouping in turn rendering (AC-3.4 / Story 3 anti-shim restoration).** In `composeRenderingInput` (src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts), group maximal runs of consecutive tool activity (tool_call/tool_result in record order, unbroken by prompts or assistant text; thinking and runtime notes do NOT break a run — record that decision in the story deviation table). Each run becomes ONE RenderingPart and ONE receipt: tools used, call count, per-call mechanical outcomes joined into a run-level account; mixed outcomes stay explicit (e.g. \"2 succeeded, 1 failed: <reason>\"), never collapsed into vague success. Outcomes remain record-derived from derived_form.metadata (mechanical stamping untouched); non-tool parts unchanged. Check src/providers/deterministic.ts join still produces sensible output with grouped parts; adjust only if the input contract changed shape. Tests: turn with prompt, call, result, call, result, text, call, result → exactly two tool-run parts (sizes 2 and 1), receipts outcome-explicit; rendering contains run accounts and does NOT contain one entry per tool message; add a mixed-outcome run case naming the failure. Ripple: confirm chunk-summary tests still pass after re-derivation (no recorded goldens exist; the double derives from input).\n- [ ] **REVERIFY-02-001 (blocking-candidate): cascadeTurnDelete missing pair-counterpart cascade.** The epic-fix-001 ruling (call/result pair is a source dependency; deleting one half is a source change for the counterpart's summary) was applied to cascadeFromMessage and cascadeMessageDelete but not cascadeTurnDelete (src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts:279-306). Cross-turn pairs are reachable (late result lands in a later turn; AC-2.8 repair rebuilds the earlier call summary). In cascadeTurnDelete, collect the paired-counterpart subjects for each deleted member message — skipping counterparts that are themselves members of the deleted turn, deduped — and clear + requeue their tool-activity summaries in the same transaction, exactly as the other two cascade paths do. Add a cross-turn regression test: call in t1, late result in t2 (summary rebuilt 'succeeded'), deleteTurn(t2) → t1's call summary cleared/requeued, rebuilds to 'unknown'.\n- [ ] **Fix 3.1 (P3): Story 3 chunk-max doc fix.** stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md line ~124: change \"max 8000\" to \"max 4400\" — tech-design DD-9, §Interfaces, and sdk.ts defaults all say 4400; the story is the outlier.\n- [ ] **Fix 3.2 (P3): TC-2.7 thinking coverage.** Add an assistant_thinking message to the existing TC-2.7 test in test/derivation-messages.test.ts: assert no work rows queued and no derivation state rows for it.\n- [ ] **Fix 3.3 (P3): Delete-side stale-straggler test.** Add a test (mutations-delete.test.ts or the natural home): claim a work item for a form on the target, delete the target (messages.deleteMessage or turns.deleteTurn), complete the stale claimed item → assert it discards (`stale_discarded`), tombstone and cascade state intact.\n- [ ] **Record Fix 1 and Fix 2** in the tech-design deviation table / story 3 deviation table as applicable: Fix 1 as a design completion (DD-4 background scheduling honors eligibility), Fix 2 as spec-compliance restoration (not a deviation).\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}}}
