{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_0126e8cb2rNu69cutmfswtkS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All verification converges. Both canonical blockers are fixed per their recorded rulings and re-verified against the current tree (per-instance seams with both-direction regression tests; deleted-read filter on both pairing reads at forms.ts:175/218; counterpart cascade in all three DD-8 callers including the `cascadeTurnDelete` gap that reverify-002 flagged, with the exact prescribed cross-turn regression test). The four retained non-blocking findings are still present exactly as recorded and do not gate. Both gates pass on my independent run: green-verify exit 0 (213 tests, immutability OK), verify-all exit 0 (240 tests).\n\n{\"outcome\":\"ready-for-closeout\",\"confirmedIssues\":[\"E02-NB-001 (retained, non-blocking, minor): mutation and requeue operations still bypass the SDK-injected clock — five runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), ...) sites re-confirmed at messages/index.ts:331,421,503 and turns/index.ts:356,433. Recorded as deliberately out of both fix batches; fix-batch-002's wake timer explicitly used the clock seam to avoid worsening it.\",\"E02-NB-003 (retained, non-blocking, observation): the deterministic provider remains the only registered named provider (providers/registry.ts registers exactly 'deterministic'). By design per DD-11 and the epic's explicit scope exclusion of real adapters; no default, fail-closed resolution confirmed.\",\"E02-NB-004 (retained, non-blocking, observation): thrown handler errors are still converted to retryable attempts (scheduler.ts:148), documented in place as a deliberate queue-protection trade-off.\",\"E02-NB-005 (retained, non-blocking, observation): attempts accounting asymmetry between terminal paths still present (scheduler.ts:126 unknown-kind stamps item.attempts vs scheduler.ts:166 blocked-source stamps item.attempts + 1). Cosmetic, undocumented.\"],\"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\":[],\"readinessAssessment\":\"All prior canonical findings are converged. EPIC-02-BLOCK-001 (mode isolation): fixed per the per-instance-scoping ruling and verified by reverify-002; fix-batch-002 touched neither sdk.ts nor shared/context.ts (only cascade.ts, compose.ts, scheduler.ts in src), the new wake timer is per-scheduler-instance state with no new process globals, and both-direction regression tests (background-then-manual, manual-then-background) are present in test/epic-fix-02.test.ts and green. EPIC-02-BLOCK-002a: findPairedBlock and findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary both join message with deleted_at IS NULL (forms.ts:175, 218). EPIC-02-BLOCK-002b and REVERIFY-02-001: the pair-counterpart cascade now exists in all three DD-8 callers — cascadeFromMessage, cascadeMessageDelete, and cascadeTurnDelete (cascade.ts:292-328: per-member counterpart collection, same-turn members skipped via memberSet, deduped, joined to the clear set on both chunk-remaining and chunk-empty paths) — and the cross-turn regression test matches reverify-002's prescribed shape exactly (call in t1, AC-2.8 late result in t2 rebuilt 'succeeded' at v2, deleteTurn(t2) clears message/m2/tool_call_summary and queues w-m2-tool_call_summary-v3, drain rebuilds 'unknown' at v3). Both unresolved items from the canonical review are closed by recorded impl-lead rulings in team-impl-log.md (cascade-scope clarification citing AC-2.8 symmetry, with TC-6.2 amended and red-manifest re-recorded; per-instance seam scoping). Fix-batch-002's other items verify: the backoff wake timer (one unref'd timer per thread, cleared by poke or newer wake, drainSettled spans the wake, manual mode untouched, recorded as tech-design deviation row E02-FIX1) with positive and negative tests; tool-run grouping in compose.ts (maximal consecutive runs into one part and one receipt, mixed outcomes explicit, recorded as E02-FIX2) with grouping and mixed-outcome tests; the three P3 items landed. Gates re-run independently on the current tree: pnpm run green-verify exit 0 (20 files, 213 tests, test-immutability OK over 27 Red-phase files) and pnpm run verify-all exit 0 (30 files, 240 tests including the LHC_PROCESS_SUITE spawned-process fixtures), matching the impl log's recorded baselines with no regression. The 002 process concern about uncommitted fix state is resolved: fix batches 1 and 2 are committed (9349b3f, 40facf7, 58d98d0). One closeout hygiene note: the working tree holds unrelated Epic 03 spec-authoring files (modified docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md plus untracked tech-design.md and test-plan.md there) and this reverify run's own 003 artifacts; the Epic 03 documents must not ride the Epic 02 closeout commit. The four retained non-blocking findings stand as recorded and do not gate closeout.\",\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to closeout: record this ready-for-closeout reverify in the team impl log, commit the Epic 02 closeout entry plus the 003-epic-reverify artifacts while excluding the Epic 03 spec files (docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/*), and carry the four retained non-blocking findings (E02-NB-001/003/004/005) forward as recorded debt — E02-NB-003 resolves naturally when a real provider adapter epic lands.\"}"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2760,"cache_read_input_tokens":113860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2760},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0237ebdd-fed4-43b7-aea6-2688595304fb","uuid":"63b82498-c03a-4bcc-bc50-713101425030","request_id":"req_011CbwKQugjCrQ8gAHjPsR7H"}
